      explain: "Create a PaymentIntent on the **server** with amount, currency, and payment method configuration (for example `automatic_payment_methods[enabled]=true`), return its **client secret** to the front end, and let Stripe.js (Payment Element) collect details and **confirm**. Statuses: `requires_payment_method` (collect or re-collect details, also after a failure), `requires_confirmation` (server-side flows), `requires_action` (customer must authenticate, for example 3D Secure, or complete a redirect), `processing` (asynchronous methods; wait), `requires_capture` (manual capture: capture or cancel), `succeeded` (fulfil), and `canceled`. Create **one PaymentIntent per order or checkout session** and reuse it on retries instead of creating new ones. **Fulfil on webhooks** (`payment_intent.succeeded`), not on the client redirect. Store the PaymentIntent id on your order to reconcile later. Pin the API version your code was written against and upgrade deliberately.",
